          "note": "Own description: the upper Anglo frame wall, 'perhaps six to eight inches thick.'"
        }
      },
      "rule": "Because the upper wall is so much thinner than the adobe below, the wall plane visibly steps in at the second floor -- a permanent record of the two building cultures meeting.",
