      "status": "drafted",
      "rule": "This is the one style in the family whose whole identity is a material change at the storey line: 24-30 in of adobe below steps to 6-10 in of frame above, and the wall plane visibly steps in 6-12 in at the second floor -- a permanent, legible record of the two building cultures meeting, not a pathology to be hidden.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "note": "Directly reverses the inherited New England Colonial rule ('one cladding material... never a decorative material change at grade or at a storey line'), which is exactly wrong for this hybrid: own hard constraint c02 says uniform wall thickness top to bottom 'removes the hybrid and produces a revival.'"
